      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "UNTETHERED SOUL (5) did well to score at Echuca two runs back, then jumped in grade and trip with a fighting eighth over 2465m at Geelong with the 59kg. Blinkers go on and ticks a few boxes with the weight drop. SPIETATA (3) caught the eye here two-back with a fast-finishing third. Went back from the awkward gate and never got into the contest with a dismal eleventh over 2040m at Seymour. Can race a touch closer and this looks much easier. Leading contender. PROPHET'S PROMISE (2) finally got off the mark at start eleven with a solid on-pace win over inferior opposition over 1900m at the Canberra Acton track. Tongue-tie goes on and can get cover from the gate. BEACHED AS BRO (4) drops a few grades for this after he failed to make an impression when fifth over 2100m at Narrandera. Place preferred.",
